def map_with_index[T: Movable & Deinitable, R: Movable & Deinitable, V: Movable & Deinitable](var function: def(var Int, var T) thin -> R, var source: V, *, start: Int = 0) -> IndexedMapIterator[T, R, _Source[V], def(var Int, var T) thin -> R] where _Source[V].Element == T:
    """Lazily map (index, owned element), using native enumerate then map.

    Construction is inert; each output moves its inputs into the non-raising callback.
    Mapping fuses exhaustion and retains owned captures, move-only results and native origins.

    Parameters:
        T: The source element type, including origins.
        R: The callback result type.
        V: The consumed native iterator or owned collection type.

    Args:
        function: The callback, borrowed or owned according to the selected overload; captures retain their native origins.
        source: The source, consumed at its current position.
        start: The first native Int index; defaults to zero.

    Returns:
        IndexedMapIterator[T, R, _Source[V], def(var Int, var T) thin -> R] with the ownership, timing and empty-input behavior described above.
    """
    var source_iter = _enumerate(_OwnedSource(source^), start=start)
    return IndexedMapIterator[T, R, _Source[V], def(var Int, var T) thin -> R](function, source_iter^, False)

